WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.800
The internet says he sold 10% of Apple for $800.

00:04.820 --> 00:05.780
Wayne calls that false.

00:06.420 --> 00:07.600
So what actually happened?

00:08.020 --> 00:11.820
Wayne drafted Apple's partnership agreement, then removed his name 12 days later.

00:12.300 --> 00:13.900
Jobs later sent him $800.

00:14.580 --> 00:17.800
Apple was not a corporation, so every partner could be personally liable.

00:18.280 --> 00:20.620
Jobs and Wozniak were young and broke.

00:21.240 --> 00:25.320
Wayne was 41, with a house, a car, and money creditors could reach.

00:26.000 --> 00:26.480
The twist?

00:27.000 --> 00:28.360
Wayne believed in Apple.

00:28.360 --> 00:28.940
None.

00:29.460 --> 00:31.480
It was the right product at the right time.

00:31.900 --> 00:37.100
He left because he expected decades of paperwork instead of building his own inventions.

00:39.120 --> 00:43.460
Lock your verdict, sell or stay, like, subscribe, and comment now.

00:44.040 --> 00:46.340
Wayne says he does not regret leaving Apple.

00:46.860 --> 00:47.720
What did he regret?

00:48.500 --> 00:50.380
He sold the original contract for $500.

00:51.020 --> 00:53.640
In 2011, it sold for $1.59 million.

00:54.360 --> 00:55.260
That I regret.

00:55.980 --> 00:57.820
So was he history's biggest fool?

00:58.340 --> 00:59.740
Or did walking away give him freedom?

